293
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:32,000
The stop stick is a tire deflation device

294
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:34,860
that we've used to stop cars.

295
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:37,640
Now, the stop stick will actually hit the ground

296
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:39,140
and the suspect will run over it,

297
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:40,400
and then it's jerked off the roadway

298
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,540
so that the other officers can go by.

299
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,340
This one here has been cut out.

300
00:16:44,341 --> 00:16:47,780
We took the outer coping off and it's a foam.

301
00:16:47,781 --> 00:16:51,540
And inside the foam are triangular quills.

302
00:16:51,541 --> 00:16:53,280
And no matter how this thing lands,

303
00:16:53,281 --> 00:16:54,880
the quills will be pointed up.

304
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,780
The quill will actually hit the tire.

305
00:16:58,781 --> 00:17:00,660
And when it does, the top of the quill,

306
00:17:00,661 --> 00:17:02,600
which is very sharp, will come out.

307
00:17:02,601 --> 00:17:04,600
And now you have a quill that's inside the tire

308
00:17:04,601 --> 00:17:07,600
that will deflate the tire at a very slow rate.

309
00:17:07,601 --> 00:17:10,300
A slow tire leak gives the driver more control

310
00:17:10,301 --> 00:17:13,040
than rapid deflation or blowout.

311
00:17:13,041 --> 00:17:16,880
Many departments use a similar device, known as a spike strip.

312
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:21,740
This accordion-like design also features hollow quills,

313
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:25,280
and like the stopstick, can be quickly deployed and retracted.

314
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:30,220
However, standing on the side of a busy highway in close proximity to a speeding pursuit

315
00:17:30,221 --> 00:17:32,280
is inherently risky business.

316
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:36,100
Sometimes they've been very useful in helping us stop the pursuit.

317
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,540
Sometimes not, you know.

